1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,125
In Telangana, an algorithm
decides who gets subsidised food.

2
00:00:05,175 --> 00:00:10,667
It matches people across government
databases, and when it finds a match,

3
00:00:10,717 --> 00:00:12,337
the family is cut off.

4
00:00:12,388 --> 00:00:18,307
In 2024, Al Jazeera reported that it
tagged Bismillah Bee's late husband,

5
00:00:18,357 --> 00:00:21,088
a rickshaw puller, as a car owner.

6
00:00:21,138 --> 00:00:26,712
Her family lost its rations, and nobody
could tell her which record did it.

7
00:00:26,762 --> 00:00:30,362
Recourse gives every family a receipt.

8
00:00:30,412 --> 00:00:33,000
This is Amina's receipt.

9
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:36,900
Amina is invented, and modelled on that case.

10
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:40,532
It says she was refused under
version two of the rules,

11
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:44,018
and that version one would
have found her eligible.

12
00:00:44,068 --> 00:00:46,606
One record decided it.

13
00:00:46,656 --> 00:00:51,991
A Toyota Innova, registered
in 2022 in Banjara Hills,

14
00:00:52,041 --> 00:00:53,718
to Syed Ali Khan.

15
00:00:53,768 --> 00:01:01,006
Amina's husband, Syed Ali, died in
2019, and the family lives in Falaknuma.

16
00:01:01,056 --> 00:01:05,793
The match scored eight thousand,
exactly at the threshold.

17
00:01:05,843 --> 00:01:10,806
The receipt lists a record only if
removing it changes the outcome.

18
00:01:10,856 --> 00:01:15,050
So if this car isn't theirs, she is eligible.

19
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:20,012
Gemini explains the receipt
in Telugu, Hindi or English.

20
00:01:20,062 --> 00:01:25,419
A guard checks every number and record
ID in the text against the receipt,

21
00:01:25,469 --> 00:01:28,586
and throws out any draft that invents one.

22
00:01:28,636 --> 00:01:30,686
Is the receipt real?

23
00:01:30,736 --> 00:01:36,607
The browser hashes it, folds its Merkle
proof into the batch root sealed on Monad

24
00:01:36,657 --> 00:01:38,874
testnet, and asks the contract.

25
00:01:38,924 --> 00:01:43,937
It also checks that the rules file
matches the hash the agency published,

26
00:01:43,987 --> 00:01:46,058
before this batch was sealed.

27
00:01:46,108 --> 00:01:51,108
Change one fact, say the
outcome, and every check fails.

28
00:01:51,158 --> 00:01:55,634
The agency can't rewrite a
decision afterwards either.

29
00:01:55,684 --> 00:01:59,040
A legal-aid worker filed
Amina's appeal on chain,

30
00:01:59,090 --> 00:02:04,134
with a letter Gemini drafted from the
receipt and from what she told them.

31
00:02:04,184 --> 00:02:07,459
The agency's answer is sealed too.

32
00:02:07,509 --> 00:02:09,674
Decision reversed.

33
00:02:09,724 --> 00:02:14,611
Anyone can open the public record,
read live from the contract.

34
00:02:14,662 --> 00:02:20,390
When the agency switched to version two,
refusals went from seven and a half percent

35
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:24,724
to almost twenty one, and most
appealed refusals were reversed.

36
00:02:24,774 --> 00:02:30,111
Because this data is synthetic, we know
version two wrongly cut off a hundred and

37
00:02:30,161 --> 00:02:31,574
twenty seven families.

38
00:02:31,624 --> 00:02:36,218
A real auditor sees the same
story in the appeal numbers.

39
00:02:36,268 --> 00:02:38,768
Two appeals are still open.

40
00:02:38,818 --> 00:02:42,386
The agency committed to
answer within thirty days,

41
00:02:42,436 --> 00:02:45,280
and if it doesn't, they show as overdue.

42
00:02:45,330 --> 00:02:51,470
The rules are public before they're used,
and every family can see what decided its

43
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:51,843
case.

44
00:02:51,893 --> 00:02:53,758
That's Recourse.
